\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {24.1}{\ignorespaces Divisors come in pairs around $\sqrt  n$. The divisors of 36 pair up as $d \cdot (36/d) = 36$: (1, 36), (2, 18), (3, 12), (4, 9) and (6, 6). Every pair has a member in the shaded part $d \le \sqrt  {36}$, so a loop up to 6 finds all nine.}}{335}{figure.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
