\newlabel{fig:totient}{{24.8}{346}{The fractions $\frac {k}{12}$ in lowest terms. The ones with denominator $d$ are the $\frac {j}{d}$ with $\gcd (j, d) = 1$, so there are $\varphi (d)$ of them, and $\sum _{d \mid n} \varphi (d) = n$: here $4 + 2 + 2 + 2 + 1 + 1 = 12$}{figure.caption.31}{}}
